# Documentation Alignment

Apply to documentation edits and to code changes that affect ownership or public APIs.

## Living Docs

- Keep [docs/architecture.md](mdc:docs/architecture.md) and [docs/overview.md](mdc:docs/overview.md) aligned with the actual implementation.
- When a change alters module ownership, public APIs, layer boundaries, or the transaction lifecycle, update those docs in the same change set when practical.

## ADRs

- When changing module ownership, public APIs, or the transaction lifecycle, update an existing ADR or create a new one under [docs/adr/](mdc:docs/adr/).
- ADRs must be written in English and state the decision, context, and consequences.

## Scope

- Do not invent large documentation rewrites unrelated to the change at hand.
- Prefer updating the specific sections that drifted from the code.
